@display("std/schema")
schema: part {
  | The kinds a [schema](#language.schemas.kinds.schema) is written with, so the format describes its own packages in Heron.
  |
  | Its surface is declared in `std/schema/package.heron`, whose types the API
  | reference renders; each export is specified where its behaviour is:
  |
  | | Export                                                        | Specified in                                                                                                               |
  | | ------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
  | | `package`                                                     | [Packages](#language.schemas.kinds.packages)                                                                               |
  | | `kind`, `accept`, `Mode`                                      | [Declaring kinds](#language.schemas.kinds.declaring), [Accept](#language.schemas.accept), [Modes](#language.schemas.modes) |
  | | `category`, `flow`, `phrasing`                                | [Categories](#language.schemas.categories)                                                                                 |
  | | `Layer`, a kind's `layer` and `extends`                       | [Layers](#language.specifications.layers)                                                                                 |
  | | `flag`, `<repeatable>`                                        | [Flags](#language.schemas.flags)                                                                                           |
  | | `annotation`                                                  | [Annotations](#language.schemas.annotations)                                                                               |
  | | `<overload>`                                                  | [Overloads](#language.schemas.overloads)                                                                                   |
  | | `Ref`                                                         | [Refs](#language.schemas.kinds.refs)                                                                                       |
  | | `language`, `Env`, `@insert`, `Insert`, `<raw>`, `@highlight` | [Highlighting](#language.schemas.highlighting), [quoting](#language.scripting.processes_and_files.quoting)                 |
  | | `Verbatim`                                                    | [a component's `exports`](#language.specifications.delivery.component_kind)                                                   |

  language_env: rule(system.interpreter) {
    where {{ a `language` is declared with `env` }}
    must {{ give the values a script's code reads to its program as the mode says: `PARAMS` as positional parameters after the script, `VARIABLES` as variables of the program's environment }}
    example {{ `std/process`'s `sh` is declared with `env = Env.PARAMS`, so `$1` in a script is its first value }}
  }
}
